
Info | updateFileDiagnostics published different from new diagnostics - file diagnostics:
File: nlg_lone_tag.l4
  Hidden: no
  Range: 8:21-8:65
  Source: parser
  Severity: DiagnosticSeverity_Warning
  Code: lint/lone-lang-tag
  Message:
    `@nlg:the` tags the wording on `over limit` as language `the`, but it is `over limit`'s only wording, and nothing else in the module makes `the` a language: no `@lang the` line declares it, and nothing has a wording in it beside one in another language.
    A tag tells apart wordings of one rule in different languages. If `the` is the first word of the sentence, write `@nlg the …` with no colon. If the wording is in `the`, add `@lang the`, or give `over limit` a wording in another language too.
